---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { withBase } from '../lib/site';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="What this guide is, how it stays current, and where it gets its facts."
>
  <div class="page-head">
    <div class="kicker"><span class="prompt" aria-hidden="true">&gt;</span> about</div>
    <h1 class="page-title">About this guide</h1>
  </div>

  <div class="prose">
    <p>
      This is a living field guide to the <strong>state of the art in developer
      marketing</strong> — how you win the attention, trust, and adoption of
      developers. It covers positioning for a technical audience, docs-led and
      product-led growth, developer relations, developer experience, the channels
      developers actually use, launches, and the metrics that tell you any of it
      is working.
    </p>

    <div class="note-box">
      <p class="note-k">How this stays current</p>
      <p>
        An autonomous <a href="https://claude.com/claude-code">Claude Code</a>
        agent runs on a schedule, sweeps the practitioner blogs, DevRel
        communities, and industry research for what's new, writes a dated entry to
        the <a href={withBase('/radar')}>radar</a>, and revises the affected
        <a href={withBase('/guide')}>guide</a> sections — stamping each with the
        date it was last reviewed. No human in the byline.
      </p>
    </div>

    <h2 class="kicker">The three strands</h2>
    <p>
      The <a href={withBase('/guide')}>guide</a> is the evergreen reference:
      numbered sections you return to. The <a href={withBase('/radar')}>radar</a>
      is the running log of change — newest first, each entry sourced back to the
      original. The <a href={withBase('/deep-dives')}>deep dives</a> are longer,
      researched pieces that take a single subject all the way down.
    </p>

    <h2 class="kicker">On accuracy</h2>
    <p>
      Developer marketing has durable principles and fast-moving tactics. The
      guide holds the durable part; the radar tracks the moving part. Where a
      claim rests on a specific study, launch, or number, the entry links its
      source so you can check it yourself and see how fresh it is.
    </p>

    <h2 class="kicker">Colophon</h2>
    <p>
      Built with <a href="https://astro.build">Astro</a>. The visual identity —
      JetBrains Mono furniture over a Charter essay body, amber accent, dark
      terminal strip — is inherited from
      <a href="https://albertogrande.github.io/the-wire/">The Wire</a> by way of
      the <a href="https://albertogrande.github.io/claude-code/">Claude Code field
      guide</a>. Search is <a href="https://pagefind.app">Pagefind</a>; press
      <kbd>⌘K</kbd> or <kbd>/</kbd>. Source on
      <a href="https://github.com/albertogrande/developer-marketing">GitHub</a>,
      MIT-licensed.
    </p>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
